'''''Tetradesmus lagerheimii''''' is a [[green alga]] in the family [[Scenedesmaceae]]. It is also known by its synonym, ''Scenedesmus acuminatus''.<ref name=AlgaeBase>{{AlgaeBase species|id=161449|name=Tetradesmus lagerheimii|access-date=2023-12-17}}</ref>

''Tetradesmus lagerheimii'' forms colonies of two, four or eight cells in a single row, with cells arranged linearly or in a somewhat zig-zag fashion. The colony is typically curved, semicircular, or contorted. Cells are spindle-shaped, arc-like, or sigmoid, 9.2–34.5(–40) μm long and 2–5.5 μm wide; the outermost side is concave; both ends taper to a point.<ref name=JohnWhitton2002>{{cite book|editor1=D. M. John |editor2=Brian A. Whitton |editor3=Alan J. Brook |title=The freshwater algal flora of the British Isles: an identification guide to freshwater and terrestrial algae|year=2002|publisher=Cambridge University Press|isbn=978-0-521-77051-4}}</ref>

It is a very common species, and is found in a variety of freshwater habitats.<ref name=AlgaeBase/>

